{"number":316,"title":"Canon patch (blocked on push scope): dedup-prune-integrity flags the VERSIONS.md row growth-dedup's own task doc mandates","body":"Working item #305 (`claudinite-growth/growth-dedup`) ran to completion — [PR #314](https://github.com/missingbulb/ClaudiniteWebsite/pull/314) merged, pruning two local rules the canon now covers — but the session's Stop-hook conformance gate then blocked on a check the growth-dedup task doc itself mandates tripping.

### What happened

`packs/claudinite-growth/tasks/growth-dedup/task.md` requires: *"Every rule this run actually prunes gets a row at the top of its pack's `VERSIONS.md` table, in the same commit as the prune."* I added two rows to this repo's `.claudinite/local/packs/claudinite-website/VERSIONS.md` in the same commit as the prune, exactly as instructed.

That commit then failed `dedup-prune-integrity` (`packs/claudinite-growth/workRules/dedup-integrity.mjs`): its shrink invariant treats **every** `.md` file under a local pack as "prose that must never grow" in a dedup-labeled commit, with no exemption for `VERSIONS.md`. But `VERSIONS.md` is the pack's changelog — by the task doc's own convention it is *supposed* to grow by exactly one row per prune, in the very commit the shrink invariant is scoped to. The two rules are in direct conflict: following the task doc's mandatory VERSIONS.md step is what makes the backstop check fire.

(This didn't block CI on PR #314, because `check_the_world.mjs` — what CI runs — explicitly excludes `scope: 'work'` rules; `dedup-prune-integrity` only runs via the session's own Stop hook, `check_the_work.mjs`. So the PR merged clean, and the conflict only surfaced afterward, blocking the session's own end-of-turn gate.)

### The fix

Exempt a pack's own `VERSIONS.md` from the shrink invariant (rule 2) — it's the record, not the pack; only the pack's prose (`RULES.md`, a skill doc) is held to "shrink, never grow". Left the canon-restatement fingerprint (rule 1) unscoped, unchanged.

**Verified before this was written:**
- `node --test packs/claudinite-growth/test/*.test.mjs` — `92 pass / 0 fail` (88 pre-existing + 4 new)
- Every new test confirmed to **fail against the unmodified source first** (2 of 4 failed, exactly the two exercising the VERSIONS.md exemption), then pass after the fix
- `node engine/checks/check_the_world.mjs` — `0 blocking` (88 pre-existing advisories, unchanged by this diff)

**Local commit:** `248afe11` — *dedup-prune-integrity: exempt a pack's own VERSIONS.md from the shrink invariant* (2 files, +66/−1)

This session cannot push it — the git proxy serves `missingbulb/Claudinite` for a fetch but `403`s a push, since this session's GitHub scope is `missingbulb/claudinitewebsite` alone (an organisation egress policy; see #59 for the same shape). Preserved here for a session with canon scope to apply.

## To apply

```sh
git checkout -b claude/dedup-versions-exempt
git apply canon-dedup-versions-exempt.patch
```

## Patch

<code>git diff HEAD~1..HEAD</code>

````diff
diff --git a/packs/claudinite-growth/test/dedup-integrity.test.mjs b/packs/claudinite-growth/test/dedup-integrity.test.mjs
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..7d9034a8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packs/claudinite-growth/test/dedup-integrity.test.mjs
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+import { test } from 'node:test';
+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
+import rule from '../workRules/dedup-integrity.mjs';
+
+const RULES = '.claudinite/local/packs/demo/RULES.md';
+const VERSIONS = '.claudinite/local/packs/demo/VERSIONS.md';
+
+// The work context the rule reads — only the members it calls.
+const work = ({ commits = ['Claudinite growth: dedup local packs'], changedFiles, files, base, added = [] }) => ({
+  branch: 'claude/some-branch',
+  onDefaultBranch: () => false,
+  commits,
+  changedFiles,
+  read: (f) => files[f] ?? null,
+  readBase: (f) => base[f] ?? null,
+  addedLines: () => added,
+});
+
+test('a dedup run that shrinks RULES.md while VERSIONS.md grows with the required log row is clean', () => {
+  const findings = rule.run(work({
+    changedFiles: [RULES, VERSIONS],
+    files: { [RULES]: 'a\nb\n', [VERSIONS]: '# log\n\n| Date | Task | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2026-08-25 | growth-dedup | Removed: ... |\n' },
+    base: { [RULES]: 'a\nb\nc\nd\n', [VERSIONS]: '# log\n\n| Date | Task | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n' },
+  }));
+  assert.deepEqual(findings, []);
+});
+
+test('a dedup run that grows RULES.md itself still fires, VERSIONS.md exemption or not', () => {
+  const findings = rule.run(work({
+    changedFiles: [RULES],
+    files: { [RULES]: 'a\nb\nc\n' },
+    base: { [RULES]: 'a\nb\n' },
+  }));
+  assert.equal(findings.length, 1);
+  assert.equal(findings[0].file, RULES);
+  assert.match(findings[0].what, /grew .*RULES\.md from 3 to 4 lines/);
+});
+
+test('VERSIONS.md alone growing in a dedup-labeled commit is never a finding', () => {
+  const findings = rule.run(work({
+    changedFiles: [VERSIONS],
+    files: { [VERSIONS]: 'one\ntwo\nthree\n' },
+    base: { [VERSIONS]: 'one\n' },
+  }));
+  assert.deepEqual(findings, []);
+});
+
+test('a non-dedup-labeled commit is never held to the shrink invariant, VERSIONS.md included', () => {
+  const findings = rule.run(work({
+    commits: ['Claudinite growth: extract lessons'],
+    changedFiles: [RULES, VERSIONS],
+    files: { [RULES]: 'a\nb\nc\n', [VERSIONS]: 'one\ntwo\n' },
+    base: { [RULES]: 'a\n', [VERSIONS]: 'one\n' },
+  }));
+  assert.deepEqual(findings, []);
+});
